Brooo 😭❤️ we'll put everything in ONE ASP.NET Web Forms program. Only one page, one small C# file, and one XML file for AdRotator.

It includes TextBox, RadioButton, DropDownList, Number input, AdRotator, Calendar, and validation controls.

## Step 1: Create the project

Create an ASP.NET Web Application (.NET Framework) using the Web Forms template. Name it `WebControlsDemo`.

## Step 2: `Default.aspx`

Replace the page code with this:

```

<%@ Page Language="C#" AutoEventWireup="true"
    CodeBehind="Default.aspx.cs"
    Inherits="WebControlsDemo.Default" %>

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>
<form id="form1" runat="server">

    <h2>Simple Web Controls</h2>

    Name:
    <asp:TextBox ID="txtName" runat="server" />
    <asp:RequiredFieldValidator ID="v1" runat="server"
        ControlToValidate="txtName"
        ErrorMessage="Enter name"
        ForeColor="Red" />
    <br /><br />

    Age:
    <asp:TextBox ID="txtAge" runat="server" TextMode="Number" />
    <asp:RequiredFieldValidator ID="v2" runat="server"
        ControlToValidate="txtAge"
        ErrorMessage="Enter age"
        ForeColor="Red" />
    <asp:RangeValidator ID="v3" runat="server"
        ControlToValidate="txtAge"
        Type="Integer" MinimumValue="1" MaximumValue="100"
        ErrorMessage="Age must be 1 to 100"
        ForeColor="Red" />
    <br /><br />

    Gender:
    <asp:RadioButtonList ID="rblGender" runat="server"
        RepeatDirection="Horizontal">
        <asp:ListItem>Male</asp:ListItem>
        <asp:ListItem>Female</asp:ListItem>
    </asp:RadioButtonList>

    Department:
    <asp:DropDownList ID="ddlDept" runat="server">
        <asp:ListItem Text="--Select--" Value="" />
        <asp:ListItem>CSE</asp:ListItem>
        <asp:ListItem>IT</asp:ListItem>
        <asp:ListItem>ECE</asp:ListItem>
    </asp:DropDownList>

    <asp:RequiredFieldValidator ID="v4" runat="server"
        ControlToValidate="ddlDept" InitialValue=""
        ErrorMessage="Select department"
        ForeColor="Red" />
    <br /><br />

    <h3>AdRotator Control</h3>
    <asp:AdRotator ID="AdRotator1" runat="server"
        AdvertisementFile="~/Ads.xml"
        Width="300px" Height="100px" />

    <h3>Calendar Control</h3>
    <asp:Calendar ID="calDate" runat="server" />

    <br />

    <asp:Button ID="btnSubmit" runat="server"
        Text="Submit" OnClick="btnSubmit_Click" />

    <br /><br />
    <asp:Label ID="lblResult" runat="server" />

</form>
</body>
</html>

```

## Step 3: `Default.aspx.cs`

Right-click `Default.aspx` → View Code, and paste this:

```

using System;

namespace WebControlsDemo
{
    public partial class Default : System.Web.UI.Page
    {
        protected void btnSubmit_Click(object sender, EventArgs e)
        {
            if (Page.IsValid)
            {
                string date = calDate.SelectedDate == DateTime.MinValue
                    ? "Not selected"
                    : calDate.SelectedDate.ToShortDateString();

                lblResult.Text =
                    "Name: " + Server.HtmlEncode(txtName.Text) +
                    "<br/>Age: " + Server.HtmlEncode(txtAge.Text) +
                    "<br/>Gender: " + Server.HtmlEncode(rblGender.SelectedValue) +
                    "<br/>Department: " + Server.HtmlEncode(ddlDept.SelectedValue) +
                    "<br/>Date: " + date;
            }
        }
    }
}

```

## Step 4: Create `Ads.xml`

Right-click the project → Add → New Item → XML File. Name it `Ads.xml`.

Paste:

```

<Advertisements>
    <Ad>
        <ImageUrl>~/Images/ad1.jpg</ImageUrl>
        <NavigateUrl>https://example.com</NavigateUrl>
        <AlternateText>Advertisement One</AlternateText>
        <Impressions>50</Impressions>
    </Ad>

    <Ad>
        <ImageUrl>~/Images/ad2.jpg</ImageUrl>
        <NavigateUrl>https://example.com</NavigateUrl>
        <AlternateText>Advertisement Two</AlternateText>
        <Impressions>50</Impressions>
    </Ad>
</Advertisements>

```

Important: Create an `Images` folder in your project. Add two image files named `ad1.jpg` and `ad2.jpg`. These are required for AdRotator to display pictures.

## Step 5: Run

Right-click `Default.aspx` → Set as Start Page → press Ctrl + F5.

You can enter your name and age, choose a gender and department, view the advertisement, select a calendar date, and press Submit. The validation controls show errors for a missing name, missing age, invalid age, or unselected department.

If your actual project namespace is not `WebControlsDemo`, replace it in both the ASPX `Inherits` value and the C# namespace to match your project.
